 "title": "GR00T N1.5 MEASURED end-to-end on Jetson AGX Orin 64GB (JetPack 6, MAXN): NVIDIA's FULL-PIPELINE TensorRT path vs our hybrid, same session",
 "date": "2026-10-12",
 "provenance": "MEASURED",
 "why": "How much of the engine-only rate survives the whole policy call, on the hybrid path (3 big engines in TRT, rest eager) vs NVIDIA's own N1.5 full-pipeline path (all 7 modules in TRT)?",
 "method": "One process, one loaded policy, alternating blocks eager/hybrid/full/hybrid/full/eager (20 timed after 5 warmup each) so session drift cancels. HYBRID = ViT/LLM/DiT TRT engines patched at the module seams . FULL = NVIDIA deployment_scripts/trt_model_forward eagle_tensorrt_forward + action_head_tensorrt_forward (ViT, LLM, vlln+vl_self_attention, state_encoder, action_encoder, DiT, action_decoder all TRT; pixel-shuffle/mlp1/embedding merge + Euler loop in torch) — module deletion skipped so the A/B can alternate. Both modes share the SAME ViT/LLM/DiT engine objects. fp16 strongly-typed engines, fixed batch-1 shapes (LLM seq 296), built from the fp16 ONNX (speed/export_onnx.sh; md5-identical across boards). Two INDEPENDENT engine builds (A, B), each with its own A/B run. Noise: torch.manual_seed(1234) per call; FULL gets the identical eager noise draw as init_actions (bf16->fp16 exact).",
